<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 18.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 18.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 10/18/96  10/11/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    214.45    210.35    92.22	90.46     96.80</p>
<p>West	    238.69    234.67    90.13	88.78     90.80</p>
<p>Total Canada  453.14    445.02    91.10	89.56     93.30</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 10/18/96: 232.55 bcf, 10/11/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 10/18/96: 264.84 bcf, 10/11/96: 264.34 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
